data: {"type":"tool-output-available","toolCallId":"call-3ee94935-961a-43ad-a27b-148ecd870de8","output":{"output":"Found 60 matches in 19 files\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/app-shell.mdx:\n  69: Both pages and extensions are loaded using the `loadLifeCycles()` function which takes the app name and component name and returns a Promise that resolves to the single-spa lifecycle object. If you look at a frontend module's entry point (`src/index.ts`), you'll see named exports that invoke either the `getAsyncLifecycle` or `getSyncLifecycle` function. These functions allow us to wrap pages and extensions into a format that can be loaded by single-spa. Essentially, the React component gets wrapped in an `openmrsComponentDecorator` that allows the framework to:\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/app-shell.mdx:\n  69: Les pages et extensions sont chargées avec la fonction `loadLifeCycles()`, qui prend le nom de l'app et le nom du composant, puis retourne une Promise résolue en objet de lifecycle single-spa. Si vous regardez le point d'entrée d'un module frontend (`src/index.ts`), vous verrez des exports nommés qui invoquent soit `getAsyncLifecycle`, soit `getSyncLifecycle`. Ces fonctions permettent d'emballer des pages et extensions dans un format chargeable par single-spa. Le composant React est essentiellement enveloppé dans un `openmrsComponentDecorator` qui permet au framework de:\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/modal-system.mdx:\n  59: import { getAsyncLifecycle } from '@openmrs/esm-framework';\n  61: export const modalComponentName = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/modal-system.mdx:\n  59: import { getAsyncLifecycle } from '@openmrs/esm-framework';\n  61: export const modalComponentName = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/core-concepts.mdx:\n  194:   `getSyncLifecycle` and `getAsyncLifecycle`, and utilities that bridge React components into single-spa lifecycles.\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/core-concepts.mdx:\n  203:   vie comme `getSyncLifecycle` et `getAsyncLifecycle`, et utilitaires qui adaptent les composants React aux cycles de vie\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/extension-system.mdx:\n  419:    import { getSyncLifecycle } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  429:    export const patientListDashboardLink = getSyncLifecycle(createDashboardLink(dashboardMeta), options);\n  432:    Note: The `getSyncLifecycle` wrapper is required to convert your React component into an extension-compatible lifecycle. The options object must include `featureName` and `moduleName`.\n  530: Extensions are rendered by following their exported lifecycle functions. The `getAsyncLifecycle` and `getSyncLifecycle` functions from `@openmrs/esm-framework` are convenience layers that export these lifecycle functions wired together with `single-spa-react`. Use `getAsyncLifecycle` for components that need to be lazy-loaded, and `getSyncLifecycle` for components that are already available synchronously.\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/extension-system.mdx:\n  419:    import { getSyncLifecycle } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  429:    export const patientListDashboardLink = getSyncLifecycle(createDashboardLink(dashboardMeta), options);\n  432:    Note : Le wrapper `getSyncLifecycle` est requis pour convertir votre composant React en un cycle de vie compatible avec les extensions. L'objet options doit inclure `featureName` et `moduleName`.\n  530: Les extensions sont rendues en suivant leurs fonctions de cycle de vie exportées. Les fonctions `getAsyncLifecycle` et `getSyncLifecycle` de `@openmrs/esm-framework` sont des couches de commodité qui exportent ces fonctions de cycle de vie, reliées ensemble avec `single-spa-react`. Utilisez `getAsyncLifecycle` pour les composants qui doivent être chargés de manière paresseuse, et `getSyncLifecycle` pour les composants déjà disponibles de manière synchrone.\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/configuration-system.mdx:\n  241: A React Hook is provided to hide the asynchronicity of config loading. The `useConfig` hook automatically determines which module's configuration to load based on the `ComponentContext`, which is set when you use `getSyncLifecycle` or `getAsyncLifecycle` with a `moduleName`.\n  246: export const hologramDoctor = getSyncLifecycle(HologramDoctor, {\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/configuration-system.mdx:\n  241: Un React Hook est fourni pour masquer l'asynchronicité du chargement de la configuration. Le hook `useConfig` détermine automatiquement quelle configuration de module charger en fonction du `ComponentContext`, qui est défini lorsque vous utilisez `getSyncLifecycle` ou `getAsyncLifecycle` avec un `moduleName`.\n  246: export const hologramDoctor = getSyncLifecycle(HologramDoctor, {\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/coding-conventions/modals.mdx:\n  84: - Export modal components with `getAsyncLifecycle` for code splitting, then register them in the `modals` section of `routes.json`. The `showModal` name must match the `name` value in `routes.json`, and `component` must match the exported lifecycle name:\n  87:   export const deleteItemModal = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/coding-conventions/modals.mdx:\n  84: - Exportez les composants modaux avec `getAsyncLifecycle` pour le code splitting, puis enregistrez-les dans la section `modals` de `routes.json`. Le nom passé à `showModal` doit correspondre à la valeur `name` dans `routes.json`, et `component` doit correspondre au nom du cycle de vie exporté :\n  87:   export const deleteItemModal = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx:\n  202: import { defineConfigSchema, getAsyncLifecycle, getSyncLifecycle } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  218: export const root = getAsyncLifecycle(() => import(\"./root.component\"), options);\n  220: export const activePrescriptionsSummary = getSyncLifecycle(ActivePrescriptionsSummary, options);\n  316: - **Sync vs async lifecycles** – `getSyncLifecycle` bundles code into the main chunk, while `getAsyncLifecycle` code-splits and loads on demand. Use each appropriately for performance. See the [Frontend modules testing guide](/docs/frontend-modules/unit-and-integration-testing) for examples and the performance notes in [Coding conventions](/docs/coding-conventions/performance).\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx:\n  194: import { defineConfigSchema, getAsyncLifecycle, getSyncLifecycle } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  210: export const root = getAsyncLifecycle(() => import(\"./root.component\"), options);\n  212: export const activePrescriptionsSummary = getSyncLifecycle(ActivePrescriptionsSummary, options);\n  307: - **Lifecycles sync vs async** – `getSyncLifecycle` embarque le code dans le bundle principal, tandis que `getAsyncLifecycle` charge à la demande. Utilisez‑les selon les besoins de performance. Voir [Tests unitaires et d’intégration](/docs/frontend-modules/unit-and-integration-testing) et les notes de performance dans [Conventions de codage](/docs/coding-conventions/performance).\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/coding-conventions/workspaces.mdx:\n  81:   export const myWorkspace = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/coding-conventions/workspaces.mdx:\n  81:   export const myWorkspace = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/workspaces/creating-workspaces.mdx:\n  119: import { getAsyncLifecycle } from '@openmrs/esm-framework';\n  128: export const gastrodynamicsWorkspace = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/workspaces/creating-workspaces.mdx:\n  119: import { getAsyncLifecycle } from '@openmrs/esm-framework';\n  128: export const gastrodynamicsWorkspace = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/coding-conventions/performance.mdx:\n  24:   - Use `getAsyncLifecycle` for modals, workspaces, secondary pages, and other components that can be loaded on demand.\n  28:   export const markPatientAliveModal = getAsyncLifecycle(() => import('./mark-patient-alive.modal'), options);\n  31:   - Use `getSyncLifecycle` for components that are already imported and need to be available immediately, such as lightweight links, action buttons, and root components that should not wait for another chunk:\n  35:   export const startVisitForm = getSyncLifecycle(startVisitFormComponent, {\n  41:   The key difference is where the component code lives. `getAsyncLifecycle` uses a dynamic import, so the bundler can create a separate chunk that O3 loads only when the component is needed. `getSyncLifecycle` wraps a component that has already been statically imported, so it stays in the main module bundle and is available as soon as the frontend module loads. Avoid making every export async by default: many tiny dynamic chunks can add extra runtime requests. Read more about the difference between static and dynamic metadata [here](/docs/migration-guides/migrate-to-core-v5).\n\n(Output was cut short: narrow the path or pattern, name a repo, or raise the limit.)","sources":[{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/app-shell.mdx","name":"app-shell.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/app-shell.mdx","name":"app-shell.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/modal-system.mdx","name":"modal-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/modal-system.mdx","name":"modal-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/core-concepts.mdx","name":"core-concepts.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/core-concepts.mdx","name":"core-concepts.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/extension-system.mdx","name":"extension-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/extension-system.mdx","name":"extension-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/configuration-system.mdx","name":"configuration-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/configuration-system.mdx","name":"configuration-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/coding-conventions/modals.mdx","name":"modals.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/coding-conventions/modals.mdx","name":"modals.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx","name":"overview.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx","name":"overview.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/coding-conventions/workspaces.mdx","name":"workspaces.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/coding-conventions/workspaces.mdx","name":"workspaces.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/workspaces/creating-workspaces.mdx","name":"creating-workspaces.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/workspaces/creating-workspaces.mdx","name":"creating-workspaces.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/coding-conventions/performance.mdx","name":"performance.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}]}}

