data: {"type":"tool-output-available","toolCallId":"call-1e3953c2-31d0-46c7-8838-87ad509fc1b2","output":{"output":"Found 30 matches in 14 files\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/app-shell.mdx:\n  69: Both pages and extensions are loaded using the `loadLifeCycles()` function which takes the app name and component name and returns a Promise that resolves to the single-spa lifecycle object. If you look at a frontend module's entry point (`src/index.ts`), you'll see named exports that invoke either the `getAsyncLifecycle` or `getSyncLifecycle` function. These functions allow us to wrap pages and extensions into a format that can be loaded by single-spa. Essentially, the React component gets wrapped in an `openmrsComponentDecorator` that allows the framework to:\n  89: When a page, extension, modal, or workspace is about to render, `loadLifeCycles()` imports the owning frontend module,\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/app-shell.mdx:\n  69: Les pages et extensions sont chargées avec la fonction `loadLifeCycles()`, qui prend le nom de l'app et le nom du composant, puis retourne une Promise résolue en objet de lifecycle single-spa. Si vous regardez le point d'entrée d'un module frontend (`src/index.ts`), vous verrez des exports nommés qui invoquent soit `getAsyncLifecycle`, soit `getSyncLifecycle`. Ces fonctions permettent d'emballer des pages et extensions dans un format chargeable par single-spa. Le composant React est essentiellement enveloppé dans un `openmrsComponentDecorator` qui permet au framework de:\n  89: Quand une page, une extension, une modale ou un workspace est sur le point d'être rendu, `loadLifeCycles()` importe le\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/modal-system.mdx:\n  59: import { getAsyncLifecycle } from '@openmrs/esm-framework';\n  61: export const modalComponentName = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/modal-system.mdx:\n  59: import { getAsyncLifecycle } from '@openmrs/esm-framework';\n  61: export const modalComponentName = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/core-concepts.mdx:\n  194:   `getSyncLifecycle` and `getAsyncLifecycle`, and utilities that bridge React components into single-spa lifecycles.\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/core-concepts.mdx:\n  203:   vie comme `getSyncLifecycle` et `getAsyncLifecycle`, et utilitaires qui adaptent les composants React aux cycles de vie\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/extension-system.mdx:\n  530: Extensions are rendered by following their exported lifecycle functions. The `getAsyncLifecycle` and `getSyncLifecycle` functions from `@openmrs/esm-framework` are convenience layers that export these lifecycle functions wired together with `single-spa-react`. Use `getAsyncLifecycle` for components that need to be lazy-loaded, and `getSyncLifecycle` for components that are already available synchronously.\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/extension-system.mdx:\n  530: Les extensions sont rendues en suivant leurs fonctions de cycle de vie exportées. Les fonctions `getAsyncLifecycle` et `getSyncLifecycle` de `@openmrs/esm-framework` sont des couches de commodité qui exportent ces fonctions de cycle de vie, reliées ensemble avec `single-spa-react`. Utilisez `getAsyncLifecycle` pour les composants qui doivent être chargés de manière paresseuse, et `getSyncLifecycle` pour les composants déjà disponibles de manière synchrone.\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/configuration-system.mdx:\n  241: A React Hook is provided to hide the asynchronicity of config loading. The `useConfig` hook automatically determines which module's configuration to load based on the `ComponentContext`, which is set when you use `getSyncLifecycle` or `getAsyncLifecycle` with a `moduleName`.\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/configuration-system.mdx:\n  241: Un React Hook est fourni pour masquer l'asynchronicité du chargement de la configuration. Le hook `useConfig` détermine automatiquement quelle configuration de module charger en fonction du `ComponentContext`, qui est défini lorsque vous utilisez `getSyncLifecycle` ou `getAsyncLifecycle` avec un `moduleName`.\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/coding-conventions/modals.mdx:\n  84: - Export modal components with `getAsyncLifecycle` for code splitting, then register them in the `modals` section of `routes.json`. The `showModal` name must match the `name` value in `routes.json`, and `component` must match the exported lifecycle name:\n  87:   export const deleteItemModal = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/coding-conventions/modals.mdx:\n  84: - Exportez les composants modaux avec `getAsyncLifecycle` pour le code splitting, puis enregistrez-les dans la section `modals` de `routes.json`. Le nom passé à `showModal` doit correspondre à la valeur `name` dans `routes.json`, et `component` doit correspondre au nom du cycle de vie exporté :\n  87:   export const deleteItemModal = getAsyncLifecycle(\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx:\n  202: import { defineConfigSchema, getAsyncLifecycle, getSyncLifecycle } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  207: export const importTranslation = require.context(\"../translations\", false, /.json$/, \"lazy\");\n  218: export const root = getAsyncLifecycle(() => import(\"./root.component\"), options);\n  316: - **Sync vs async lifecycles** – `getSyncLifecycle` bundles code into the main chunk, while `getAsyncLifecycle` code-splits and loads on demand. Use each appropriately for performance. See the [Frontend modules testing guide](/docs/frontend-modules/unit-and-integration-testing) for examples and the performance notes in [Coding conventions](/docs/coding-conventions/performance).\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx:\n  194: import { defineConfigSchema, getAsyncLifecycle, getSyncLifecycle } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n  199: export const importTranslation = require.context(\"../translations\", false, /.json$/, \"lazy\");\n  210: export const root = getAsyncLifecycle(() => import(\"./root.component\"), options);\n\n(Output was cut short: narrow the path or pattern, name a repo, or raise the limit.)","sources":[{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/app-shell.mdx","name":"app-shell.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/app-shell.mdx","name":"app-shell.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/modal-system.mdx","name":"modal-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/modal-system.mdx","name":"modal-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/core-concepts.mdx","name":"core-concepts.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/core-concepts.mdx","name":"core-concepts.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/extension-system.mdx","name":"extension-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/extension-system.mdx","name":"extension-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/configuration-system.mdx","name":"configuration-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/configuration-system.mdx","name":"configuration-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/coding-conventions/modals.mdx","name":"modals.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/coding-conventions/modals.mdx","name":"modals.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx","name":"overview.mdx","revision":"HEAD"},{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/fr-FR/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx","name":"overview.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}]}}

