data: {"type":"data-source","data":{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/extension-system.mdx","name":"extension-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}}

data: {"type":"tool-output-available","toolCallId":"call-8be5ff04-b519-44fe-93f1-a082538681b7","output":{"output":"<repo>github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs</repo>\n<path>content/en-US/docs/extension-system.mdx</path>\n<url>undefined</url>\n<content>\n520: \n521: - **attached**: Set via code using `attach()` (or declaratively via the `slot`/`slots` property in `routes.json`). Note: `detach()` is deprecated.\n522: - **configured**: Set via administrator configuration using the `add` and `remove` arrays\n523: - **assigned**: Computed by merging attached and configured extensions, then filtering based on privileges, feature flags, and connectivity (`online`/`offline` flags)\n524: - **connected**: (Deprecated term) This is the same as \"assigned\" after filtering—extensions that are actually rendered\n525: \n526: The runtime uses the \"assigned\" state to determine which extensions to render. The filtering happens automatically based on user privileges, enabled feature flags, and connectivity state.\n527: \n528: ### Rendering\n529: \n530: Extensions are rendered by following their exported lifecycle functions. The `getAsyncLifecycle` and `getSyncLifecycle` functions from `@openmrs/esm-framework` are convenience layers that export these lifecycle functions wired together with `single-spa-react`. Use `getAsyncLifecycle` for components that need to be lazy-loaded, and `getSyncLifecycle` for components that are already available synchronously.\n531: \n532: In a nutshell:\n533: \n534: 1. When the component should be rendered, the `load` function is evaluated. If it returns a `Promise` (via an asynchronously loaded `import()`), the system waits for the component to be available.\n535: 2. The component is wrapped with lifecycle functions provided by `single-spa-react`.\n536: 3. The lifecycle functions (`bootstrap`, `mount`, `unmount`, and `update`) are exported and managed by Single-SPA.\n537: \n538: These lifecycle functions are not magic - theoretically you could write them on your own, however, since the single-spa ecosystem already provides convenience wrappers such as `single-spa-react` for many frameworks we don’t recommend it.\n539: \n540: Before rendering, two additional factors are evaluated:\n541: \n542: 1. **Connectivity mode**: Whether the extension should render based on the current online/offline state\n543: 2. **Component props**: What data and services should be passed to the rendered component\n544: \n\n(Showing lines 520-544 of 558. Use offset=545 to continue.)\n</content>","sources":[{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/extension-system.mdx","name":"extension-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}]}}

